;; The native check's known differences (bin/repr-cpp native-check; doc/cpp/NATIVE.md, "The check"): a file whose forms read by the native
;; parser differ from the forms read from the oracle's dump, NAME (as the list names it, under its corpus: gxx-dg/, samples/, native/) -> its
;; class. Every class is a fact of clang's Sema the native reader does not compute (CX11: a parser with the names' kinds, no Sema):
;;   :defaulted-noexcept  a defaulted special member's or comparison's exception specification, which clang evaluates when the member is
;;                        used (M m; uses M() = default, which then prints noexcept); unused, it stays unevaluated (no noexcept)
;;   :init-list-form      an initializer list's semantic form in clang's tree: an aggregate's elided braces restored, the members a
;;                        designator skips value-initialized (the converter writes such a list as its text)
;;   :ctad                a class template's arguments deduced from an initializer (A a(b); declares an A<int>)
;;   :builtin-signature   a library function's redeclaration with the attributes of clang's builtin or of the header's declaration it
;;                        redeclares (_Nonnull on a parameter), a builtin's call rewritten (__sync_fetch_and_add to its sized _8)
;;   :dependent-member    a member named in a class template's member function, which clang leaves unresolved (an UnresolvedMemberExpr:
;;                        the converter writes its text)
;;   :implicit-argument   a call's argument clang adds (a default argument of the operator new a new-expression calls)
;;   :clang-recovery      an ill-formed construct clang reads by its error recovery (inline template <int> void foo ())
;;   :deduced-type        a function's deduced return type, which clang's tree holds in the function's type (auto f() { return [=]
;;                        (int b) {...}; }: a closure type, which the converter writes as the function's text)
;;   :native-decline      a construct the parser declines (a NativeDecline: its text), clang reads (not a Sema fact: the grammar's gap)
;; Since cpp-sema (doc/cpp/NATIVE.md §8) the parser computes the classes' Sema facts as clang does (arbace.repr.cpp.sema) where they
;; are bounded; the classes stay for the cases it leaves to clang (a type it does not know, a guide it cannot choose, clang's
;; table of library builtins).
;; A file the run finds the same that is listed here is an improvement (said, not a failure); one that differs and is not listed fails.
;; Read with the Clojure reader.
;; (dump1.C's :native-decline is fixed since the tree check, NATIVE.md §9: a class defined outside its enclosing class sees the
;; enclosing class's names.)
{"gxx-dg/lto/pr45679-1_1.C" :builtin-signature}
